\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thy way, not mine, O Lord,
\par However dark it be!
\par Lead me by Thine own hand;
\par Choose out the path for me.
\par Smooth let it be or rough,
\par It will be still the best;
\par Winding or straight, it leads
\par Right onward to Thy rest.\tab\tab 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 2. I dare not choose my lot;
\par I would not, if I might:
\par Choose Thou for me, my God;
\par So shall I walk aright.
\par The kingdom that I seek 
\par Is Thine; so let the way
\par That leads to it be Thine,
\par Else I must surely stray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Take Thou my cup, and it
\par With joy or sorrow fill
\par As best to thee may seem;
\par Choose Thou my good and ill.
\par Not mine, not mine the choice
\par In things or great or small;
\par Be thou my Guide, my Strength, 
\par My Wisdom, and my all. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

